// The same refusal as module_nameres_transit, from the other side of the load
// order: a module loaded AFTER the one that folded the names.
//
// It is the control that says what decides the answer. Reaching a folded name
// through its module's qualifier used to depend on which module was loaded
// first -- refused from the root and from anything loaded before the folding
// module, accepted from anything loaded after it. Importing modulehide first is
// what puts it ahead of modulehidelate in that order, and the reach is refused
// all the same, because what the check reads is the binding's own visibility.
//
// Its one diagnostic is reported against modulehidelate.cone, so the annotation
// lives there and this file has none.
//
// The imported modules are modulehide.cone, modulehidelate.cone and, through
// modulehide, modulesub.cone.

mod module_nameres_transit_late;

import modulehide;
import modulehidelate;

fn viaLate() i64 {
  modulehidelate.viaMid(1i64) + modulehide.hidOwn(2i64);
}
